{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a9cf5575-0e56-41bc-a630-7b8da7730770","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5e88b04ab9583cf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9004-unrgr3y_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9004-E001.md","content":"# Disconnected environment guidance for KServe raw deployment mode\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a disconnected-install guide for KServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. The KServe capability already exists and works in disconnected clusters; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams currently rediscover the required steps (which images to mirror, which operators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install) from private gists. Source material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and technical review work — no code, operator, or default-configuration changes.\n\n## Scope\n\nAuthor a new disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode with the following content outline:\n\n1. **Prerequisites** — cluster and environment requirements for an air-gapped install using raw deployment mode (plain Deployments/Services, no mesh dependency).\n2. **Operator configuration** — which operators are required and which are skipped in raw deployment mode on a disconnected cluster (Service Mesh and Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only dependencies and are not needed).\n3. **Image-mirroring reference** — the complete list of required images to mirror and the procedure for deriving the digest list per release.\n4. **Validation steps** — how to verify a correct air-gapped install (e.g., InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode).\n5. **Troubleshooting section** — coverage of the three most common field-reported failure modes: image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n\nOut of scope: any code, operator, or default-configuration change; serverless mode disconnected support.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **Given** a disconnected cluster, **when** a user follows the guide, **then** they can complete a KServe raw deployment mode install — measured by the guide covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps (HLR-1).\n- **Given** a target release, **when** a user prepares the mirror, **then** the guide's image-mirroring reference lists all required images and explains how to derive the digest list for that release — measured by a technical reviewer confirming the list is complete for a current release (HLR-2).\n- **Given** one of the three field-reported failure modes (image pull errors, missing runtime, storage-initializer misconfiguration), **when** a user consults the troubleshooting section, **then** diagnostic and remediation steps are present — measured by review against field enablement source material (HLR-3).\n- **Technical accuracy validation (mandatory):** all statements about KServe raw deployment mode, its dependencies, and disconnected-environment behavior are validated against the KServe architecture context (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`) — in particular that raw deployment uses plain Deployments/Services without mesh dependency, that Service Mesh/Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only, and that model execution depends on the serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit).\n- **Technically reviewed against implementation:** the published guide is reviewed and signed off by the serving engineering team to confirm it matches actual product behavior.\n- No code, operator, or default-configuration changes are introduced as part of this work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | Disconnected install guide (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation steps) — full epic scope |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Image-mirroring reference section of the guide |\n| HLR-3 | P2 | Troubleshooting section covering the three field-reported failure modes |\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":18699,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a118cf74a0583dbc","agent_id":"a2762cf8601011a0a","session_id":"1408b023-5547-4414-b80e-ccfb4877e639","uuid":"136007cb-2fb0-4f52-8814-fb5eede2967a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:19:29.915Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9004"}
