{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9808aca18ccf99e8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9004-E001\n3\ttitle: Disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9004\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Disconnected environment guidance for KServe raw deployment mode\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a disconnected-install guide for KServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. The KServe capability already exists and works in disconnected clusters; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams currently rediscover the required steps (which images to mirror, which operators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install) from private gists. Source material exists in field enablement docs; this epic is authoring and technical review work — no code, operator, or default-configuration changes.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\tAuthor a new disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode with the following content outline:\n38\t\n39\t1. **Prerequisites** — cluster and environment requirements for an air-gapped install using raw deployment mode (plain Deployments/Services, no mesh dependency).\n40\t2. **Operator configuration** — which operators are required and which are skipped in raw deployment mode on a disconnected cluster (Service Mesh and Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only dependencies and are not needed).\n41\t3. **Image-mirroring reference** — the complete list of required images to mirror and the procedure for deriving the digest list per release.\n42\t4. **Validation steps** — how to verify a correct air-gapped install (e.g., InferenceService readiness in raw deployment mode).\n43\t5. **Troubleshooting section** — coverage of the three most common field-reported failure modes: image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration.\n44\t\n45\tOut of scope: any code, operator, or default-configuration change; serverless mode disconnected support.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- **Given** a disconnected cluster, **when** a user follows the guide, **then** they can complete a KServe raw deployment mode install — measured by the guide covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps (HLR-1).\n50\t- **Given** a target release, **when** a user prepares the mirror, **then** the guide's image-mirroring reference lists all required images and explains how to derive the digest list for that release — measured by a technical reviewer confirming the list is complete for a current release (HLR-2).\n51\t- **Given** one of the three field-reported failure modes (image pull errors, missing runtime, storage-initializer misconfiguration), **when** a user consults the troubleshooting section, **then** diagnostic and remediation steps are present — measured by review against field enablement source material (HLR-3).\n52\t- **Technical accuracy validation (mandatory):** all statements about KServe raw deployment mode, its dependencies, and disconnected-environment behavior are validated against the KServe architecture context (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`) — in particular that raw deployment uses plain Deployments/Services without mesh dependency, that Service Mesh/Serverless operators are serverless-mode-only, and that model execution depends on the serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit).\n53\t- **Technically reviewed against implementation:** the published guide is reviewed and signed off by the serving engineering team to confirm it matches actual product behavior.\n54\t- No code, operator, or default-configuration changes are introduced as part of this work.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n59\t|-----|----------|----------|\n60\t| HLR-1 | P1 | Disconnected install guide (prerequisites, operator configuration, validation steps) — full epic scope |\n61\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Image-mirroring reference section of the guide |\n62\t| HLR-3 | P2 | Troubleshooting section covering the three field-reported failure modes |\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ea7aa31686b8494","agent_id":"a3e2b6d815bd55b93","session_id":"1408b023-5547-4414-b80e-ccfb4877e639","uuid":"2c4acd8f-f3bd-4ab3-970c-17f24a4507f2","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:21:34.237Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9808aca18ccf99e8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
