{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a03441426b652dae","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9004\n3\ttitle: Disconnected environment guidance for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- disconnected\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tRaw deployment mode is the recommended KServe path for disconnected clusters,\n15\tbut our documentation only covers serverless mode installs. Field teams keep\n16\trediscovering the same steps — which images to mirror, which operators to skip,\n17\thow to verify an air-gapped install — in private gists. Nothing in this\n18\tstrategy changes product behavior; the capability exists and works. The gap is\n19\tentirely published guidance.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1 | P1 | A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode exists in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps. |\n26\t| HLR-2 | P1 | The guide includes a complete image-mirroring reference (required images and how to derive the digest list per release). |\n27\t| HLR-3 | P2 | A troubleshooting section covers the three most common field-reported failure modes (image pull errors, missing runtime, storage-initializer misconfiguration). |\n28\t\n29\t## Affected Components\n30\t\n31\t- KServe\n32\t- Documentation\n33\t\n34\t## Out of Scope\n35\t\n36\t- Any code, operator, or default-configuration change\n37\t- Serverless mode disconnected support\n38\t\n39\t## Open Questions\n40\t\n41\tNone — source material exists in field enablement docs; this is authoring and\n42\ttechnical review work.\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8fa9fb03e35e581","agent_id":"ad0e239dc78b6743f","session_id":"1408b023-5547-4414-b80e-ccfb4877e639","uuid":"9ad0b080-18